BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d3-1@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T195527Z
DTSTART:20270105T190000Z
DTEND:20270105T200500Z
SUMMARY:📸 Hoʻomaluhia Botanical Garden
DESCRIPTION:Opens at 9:00. Drive in\, park by the lake for mountain photos\
 , and walk a short stretch. Skipping Byodo-In this time\, so you can linge
 r here.\n\n🚗 Getting there: about 35 min drive from Waikīkī rental of
 fice (sample location) (24 km)\n\n📍 Hoʻomaluhia Botanical Garden\, 45-
 680 Luluku Rd\, Kāneʻohe\n🧭 https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&de
 stination=Ho%CA%BBomaluhia%20Botanical%20Garden
LOCATION:Hoʻomaluhia Botanical Garden\, 45-680 Luluku Rd\, Kāneʻohe
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=Ho%CA%BBomaluhia%20B
 otanical%20Garden
GEO:21.3882747;-157.8070148
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS="45-680 Luluku Rd, Kāneʻo
 he";X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Hoʻomaluhia Botanical Garden":geo:21.3882
 747,-157.8070148
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d3-2@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T195527Z
DTSTART:20270105T210000Z
DTEND:20270105T233000Z
SUMMARY:🎟️ Kualoa Ranch Jurassic Adventure
DESCRIPTION:Check in at the ranch around 10:40. Ride an off-road vehicle in
 to the Kualoa\, Hakipuʻu and Kaʻaʻawa valleys to see filming spots from
  Jurassic Park\, Jurassic World and more. Bumpy ride\, only short walks. B
 ook your slot ahead.\n\n🚗 Getting there: about 30 min drive from Hoʻom
 aluhia Botanical Garden (20 km)\n\n📍 Kualoa Ranch\, 49-560 Kamehameha H
 wy\, Kāneʻohe\n🧭 https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=K
 ualoa%20Ranch\nKualoa official site: https://www.kualoa.com/tours/
LOCATION:Kualoa Ranch\, 49-560 Kamehameha Hwy\, Kāneʻohe
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=Kualoa%20Ranch
GEO:21.5208318;-157.8372577
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS="49-560 Kamehameha Hwy, Kā
 neʻohe";X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Kualoa Ranch":geo:21.5208318,-157.837
 2577
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d3-3@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T195527Z
DTSTART:20270106T000500Z
DTEND:20270106T004000Z
SUMMARY:🍽️ Giovanni's garlic shrimp
DESCRIPTION:Lunch. If the line is too long\, try Romy's or Fumi's next door
 . Then head west on Kamehameha Hwy\; just glance at Shark's Cove and Waime
 a Bay from the car: North Shore surf is big on winter afternoons\, so no d
 edicated stops.\n\n🚗 Getting there: about 35 min drive from Kualoa Ranc
 h (25 km)\n\n📍 Giovanni's Shrimp Truck\, Kahuku\, 56-505 Kamehameha Hwy
 \, Kahuku\n🧭 https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=Giovann
 i's%20Shrimp%20Truck%2C%20Kahuku
LOCATION:Giovanni's Shrimp Truck\, Kahuku\, 56-505 Kamehameha Hwy\, Kahuku
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=Giovanni's%20Shrimp%
 20Truck%2C%20Kahuku
GEO:21.677198;-157.9484211
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS="56-505 Kamehameha Hwy, Kah
 uku";X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Giovanni's Shrimp Truck, Kahuku":geo:21.6
 77198,-157.9484211
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d3-4@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T195527Z
DTSTART:20270106T010500Z
DTEND:20270106T012000Z
SUMMARY:📸 Turtle watching at Laniakea
DESCRIPTION:Turtles often haul out to bask in the afternoon\; watch from sh
 ore for 15 min and keep your distance. Roadside parking is tight\; if ther
 e's no spot\, go straight to Dole.\n\n🚗 Getting there: about 25 min dri
 ve from Giovanni's Shrimp Truck (20 km)\n\n📍 Laniakea Beach\, Kamehameh
 a Hwy\, Haleʻiwa\n🧭 https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination
 =Laniakea%20Beach
LOCATION:Laniakea Beach\, Kamehameha Hwy\, Haleʻiwa
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=Laniakea%20Beach
GEO:21.6187;-158.0853
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS="Kamehameha Hwy, Haleʻiwa"
 ;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Laniakea Beach":geo:21.6187,-158.0853
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d3-5@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T195527Z
DTSTART:20270106T014000Z
DTEND:20270106T033000Z
SUMMARY:🎟️ Dole Plantation: train + maze
DESCRIPTION:Ride the Pineapple Express train first (~20 min\, roughly every
  10 min\; the official site suggests 1 hour including the pineapple-cuttin
 g demo)\, then the Pineapple Garden Maze (40 min on average)\, and finish 
 with Dole Whip. Park hours 9:30–17:30\; the last train and last maze ent
 ry aren't listed online\, so call 808-621-8408 before you go. If the last 
 train is early\, do the maze first.\n\n🚗 Getting there: about 15 min dr
 ive from Laniakea Beach (15 km)\n\n📍 Dole Plantation\, 64-1550 Kamehame
 ha Hwy\, Wahiawā\n🧭 https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination
 =Dole%20Plantation\nDole Plantation official site: https://www.doleplantat
 ion.com/
LOCATION:Dole Plantation\, 64-1550 Kamehameha Hwy\, Wahiawā
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=Dole%20Plantation
GEO:21.5259081;-158.0378039
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS="64-1550 Kamehameha Hwy, Wa
 hiawā";X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Dole Plantation":geo:21.5259081,-158.0
 378039
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
